gulations, and the National Standards for Residential Care Settings for Older People in Ireland set out what people should expect. Disability services are measured against the National Standards for Residential Services for Children and Adults with Disabilities. Certain events are notifiable to HIQA, and a provider must submit information as required. Always work from the current published standards and regulations.</p><h2>Inside the EU, under GDPR</h2><p>Because Ireland is an EU member, data residency matters and is easy to answer here. Quickler hosts every record on EU servers in Germany and handles it in line with GDPR. Nothing leaves the EU, which keeps the data-residency answer simple for an Irish provider keeping resident and staff data within the bloc. Pricing is available in euro. For the wider Irish picture, see field compliance software for Ireland.</p><h2>How quickler runs it</h2><p>Quickler turns a recurring audit or a whole standards area into a workflow that runs over the WhatsApp Business API. The person in charge or a nominated staff member walks the centre and answers each prompt in their existing WhatsApp chat, with text, a voice note or a photo tied to the standard it evidences. Voice notes are transcribed automatically. The report and improvement plan generate themselves, and a provider running several designated centres sees each one's position on a single dashboard.</p><h2>Pricing</h2><p>Pricing is only for active users: [[price:bundles]]. An active user is someone who completed at least two workflows that month, so you can add every manager, nurse, care worker and bank worker across the provider and pay only for who actually files something. Dormant users are free and pricing is available in euro. The free tier is 20 reports a month and up to 10 photos per report, no card and no trial clock.</p><h2>What quickler is not</h2><p>Quickler is not a care record, care management, eMAR or clinical system, and holds no resident care data. It captures the audit walk and the evidence around it: photos of the setting, observations against the standards, the state of records at the point of check. For medication and care plans it records that the check was done and captures the evidence, without copying a resident's personal or clinical data into quickler. Care plans, medication administration records and personal care logs stay in your care planning system, which remains the single source of truth. Quickler is the audit and evidence layer that sits alongside the care system.</p><p>Quickler is not affiliated with or endorsed by HIQA, and whether your evidence satisfies an inspection is a judgement for you and your inspector. This page is general information, not regulatory advice; always work from the current published National Standards and regulations.</p><h2>Related guides</h2><ul><li><a href=\"/pages/field-compliance-software-ireland.html\">Field compliance software for Ireland</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/care-home-compliance-software-uk.html\">Care home compliance software UK</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/care-home-compliance-software-scotland.html\">Care home compliance software Scotland</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/five-regulators-one-job-british-isles.html\">Five regulators, one job</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/medication-storage-audit-care-uk.html\">Medication storage audit</a></li></ul>",
